+└── docs/
+    └── SPRINT_0_SETUP.md  # This file
+```
+
+---
+
+## How to Start
+
+### 1. Start Databases
+
+```bash
+# Start PostgreSQL and Redis
+docker-compose up -d
+
+# Verify services
+docker-compose ps
+# Expected: postgres, redis, pgadmin all "Up"
+
+# Access pgAdmin at http://localhost:5050
+# (email: admin@flowstudio.local, password: admin)
+```
+
+### 2. Install Dependencies
+
+```bash
+# Install all workspaces
+npm install
+
+# Or specific workspace
+npm install --workspace=@flowstudio/api
+```
+
+### 3. Initialize Database
+
+```bash
+# Generate Prisma client
+npm run db:generate --workspace=@flowstudio/api
+
+# Push schema to PostgreSQL
+npm run db:push --workspace=@flowstudio/api
+
+# (Optional) Launch Prisma Studio
+npm run db:studio --workspace=@flowstudio/api
+# Opens http://localhost:5555 — visual DB editor
+```
+
+### 4. Start API Server
+
+```bash
+# Development mode with watch
+npm run start:dev --workspace=@flowstudio/api
+
+# Expected output:
+# [Nest] <timestamp>  LOG [Bootstrap] FlowStudio API running on port 3000
+# [Nest] <timestamp>  LOG [PrismaService] ✅ Database connected
+```
+
+### 5. Test Health Endpoint
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:3000/health
+# Expected:
+# {
+#   "status": "healthy",
+#   "timestamp": "2026-08-08T...",
+#   "database": "connected",
+#   "environment": "development"
+# }
+```
+
+### 6. (Optional) Start Frontend
+
+```bash
+npm run dev --workspace=@flowstudio/web
+# Frontend on http://localhost:3100
+```
+
+---
+
+## Exit Criteria for Sprint 0 ✅
+
+All completed:
+
+- [x] PostgreSQL running in docker-compose with persistent volume
+- [x] Redis running in docker-compose with persistent volume
+- [x] Prisma schema complete with all models
+- [x] NestJS API scaffold with health endpoint
+- [x] Database connection validation
+- [x] Shared packages (IR, Registry) initialized
+- [x] TypeScript configurations for all apps
+- [x] Development environment (.env.local) ready
+- [x] Root package.json with workspaces
+- [x] All services boot without errors
+
+---
+
+## Next Steps → Sprint 1
+
+Sprint 1 will implement the **AI Gateway Layer**:
+
+1. **AiGatewayService** — Model registry and router logic
+2. **Admin page** — `/admin/models` to register new models
+3. **Model registration** — `POST /api/admin/models`
+4. **First real model** — Register Flux (IMAGE model)
+5. **Chat endpoint** — `POST /api/chat` for TEXT analysis
+6. **Ledger integration** — Record cost = 0 for text
+
+**Exit Criteria for Sprint 1:**
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/chat \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"text": "نانوایی سنگک یک ویدیو برای تبلیغ بخواهد"}'
+→ 200 { "id": "gen_123", "briefId": "brief_123", "cost": 0 }
+```
+
+---
+
+## Important Notes
+
+### Environment Setup
+- **Development**: Uses `.env.local` (git-ignored)
+- **Example**: See `.env.example` for all required variables
+- **Database**: PostgreSQL at `localhost:5432` (user: `flowstudio`)
+- **Redis**: At `localhost:6379` (no auth in dev)
+
+### Project Structure Philosophy
+- **Monorepo**: Apps and packages share types via npm workspaces
+- **Separation**: Code is copied from wbc, not reused via imports
+- **Modality**: Abstract ModelAdapter allows plugging new models
+- **IR**: All data flows through intermediate representation types
+
+### Prisma Best Practices
+- **Schema**: In `prisma/schema.prisma`
+- **Migrations**: Auto-create via `db push` (dev) or `migrate` (production)
+- **Client**: Auto-generated, use via `PrismaService`
+- **Studio**: Visual editor at `localhost:5555`
+
+---
+
+## Files Not Yet Created (For Future Sprints)
+
+- `apps/api/src/modules/` — Feature modules (Sprint 1+)
+- `apps/engine/` — Worker for async jobs (Sprint 6)
+- `apps/media/` — Video transcoding (Sprint 8)
+- `deploy/k8s/` — Kubernetes manifests (future)
+- `docs/00` through `docs/70` — Detailed specifications (existing in project)
+
+---
+
+**Status:** ✅ **READY FOR SPRINT 1**  
+**Run Tests:** `npm run health` (or manual curl as shown above)  
+**Questions?** Check `docs/00` through `docs/70` for detailed architecture
